WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.240
(SNIFFLING)

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.760
Felix, I know
we've never once talked about

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.440
having a family before, but...

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.440
I know, it feels
like the kind of thing

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.120
you just jump into
with both feet...

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.480
and nary a plan.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.720
Felix and I
will give them sanctuary.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.840
(SPITS)

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.080
Can I get a quick word
with you two?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.160
(SUGAR RUSH RACERS CHEERING)

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.560
Look, I get it.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.160
You've been married six years,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.720
you're looking to
spice things up...

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.880
but trust me,
adopting 15 children

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.640
is the wrong kind of spice.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.360
Those things
are basically feral.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.360
Pardon me, sir, but those
youngsters are lambs.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.400
Lost little lambs in need of
two kind, caring shepherds.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.560
That's right.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.520
Besides,
how hard can parenting be?

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.360
You treat the child
like your best friend...

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.240
you give them
everything they want...

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.240
and you just love their little
socks off. Right, Tammy?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.840
Darn-tootin'.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.520
-(GIRL SCREAMING)
-FELIX: (GASPS) Huh?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.600
(FELIX GASPS)

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.680
RACER KID: Come and get it.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.760
CANDLEHEAD:
Get your own candle.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.240
Hey, Mom,
why does your lame TV

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.960
only have one channel?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.840
(CHUCKLES) Well,
hate to say I told ya...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.040
Ow!

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.680
(SURGE PROTECTOR GROANS)

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.240
(ARCADE SOUNDS)

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.040
(RALPH SIGHS)

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.120
Hey, Tapper?

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.280
No, Ralph.
I haven't seen Vanellope.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.520
Not since the last time
you asked me 30 seconds ago.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.760
Sorry.
I'm just worried about her.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.720
She's glitching like crazy,
and acting super insecure.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.840
Oh. And get this, she said...

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.520
being friends with me
wasn't enough for her.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.320
Not enough?
I'm a great friend!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.920
Right, Tapper? Right?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.160
I'm sorry.
Who's acting insecure?

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.440
Ralph, come on.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.400
The kid just lost her game.
Give her a break.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.760
(STOOL SCRAPES)

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.520
There you are... Oh.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:50.800
Hey, Ralph.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.200
Hey, Felix. Since when do you
drink root beer?

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.480
Since tonight.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.280
Yeah, I hear you, buddy.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.720
Hey, listen. This one was
supposed to be for Vanellope.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.880
I guess you can have it.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.640
Doesn't look like
she's coming.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.800
Thanks.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.400
You know,
I can't help but think

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.680
this whole mess is somehow...

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.200
partially my fault.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.480
It figures.
Just when my life was perfect.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.120
Mine was, too.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.680
But, hey,
now I'm a father of 15.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.400
Isn't that just a blessing?

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.600
(SLURPS, GULPING)

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.240
(COUGHING, EXCLAIMS)

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.000
Eeeee-oh-boy!

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.720
Wait. What'd you say, Felix?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.840
Um, isn't that
just a blessing?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.480
No, the weird sound thing.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.880
Oh. Eeeee-oh-boy?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.000
Yeah. (SOFTLY) Eee-oh...

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.080
Sorry, say it again?

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.080
-Eeeee-oh-boy.
-Eeeee-oh-boy!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.200
-Eee-oh-boy!
-Eee-boy! Say it again?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.400
-Eeeee-oh-boy!
-Eeeee-oh-boy.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.920
-Eeeee-oh-boy...
-eboy! eboy! eboy!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.200
-eboy? eboy?
-eboy.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.640
Yeah.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.040
Um, what are you getting
at there, Ralph?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.640
That kid out in the arcade

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.200
said there was
a steering wheel part...

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.560
on the Internet, it's
something called eboy or...

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.960
ebay!
That's it, it was ebay!

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.520
Ralph, are you thinking about

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.680
going to the Internet
and finding that part?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.200
Getting that part's
the only thing

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.120
that's gonna fix the game
and that's the only thing

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.040
that's gonna make
Vanellope happy again.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.760
And if Sugar Rush is fixed,

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.000
all those lovable scamps
living in my house...

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.280
and destroying my sanity

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.640
will have homes
of their own again!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.000
Ralph, this is an important
mission. A noble mission!

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.120
I will cover for you.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.320
Thanks, pal.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.360
Ralph, what about your tab?
You owe me for the root beer.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.080
Oh, Felix is gonna
cover for me.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.600
Drinks on the house,
everybody! Felix is paying.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.720
-(ALL CHEERING)
-RYU: Shoryuken!

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.240
Eeeee-oh-boy.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.760
(GROANS)

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.480
-Boo!
-(GLITCHY SCREAMING)

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.400
Ralph, what is wrong with you?

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.160
Start churning butter

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.640
and put on your church shoes,
little sister...

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.200
'cause we're about to
blast off!

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.920
What are you
even talking about?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Oh, we're going to
the Internet.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.080
(EXCLAIMS) What?

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.680
Yeah, to find the part
to fix your game.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:58.840
No way!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.000
Yeah, I probably
should've just said,

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.840
"We're going to the Internet."
We're going to the Internet!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.040
VANELLOPE: Yeah, we are!

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.480
Hey, Surge, (SIGHS)
are we glad to see you.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.120
We want to report
some malfeasance

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.280
over by the Whac-A-Mole.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.200
Yeah, we saw some undesirables

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.600
causing a real donnybrook
over there.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.840
(SCOFFS) Oh, heck no.
Not on my watch.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.440
Appreciate the tip.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.640
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.240
So, all we gotta do
is find this eboy place.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.040
-ebay.
-Right, ebay.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.160
So we go there,
get the steering wheel...

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.960
we have it delivered to Litwak
before Friday.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.240
He'll fix your game.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.000
Everything goes back
to the way it was.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.840
Boom! Happily ever after.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.320
VANELLOPE:
This is a shockingly sound,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.960
well-thought-out idea
for you, Ralph.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.160
No offense.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.640
I know. And none taken.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.800
VANELLOPE: Ooh, here it comes.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.840
Ladies and gentlemen,
boys and girls...

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.440
I give you the Internet!

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.640
RALPH: Huh.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.880
The Internet is
not nearly as impressive

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.480
as how Sonic described it.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.920
Yeah, I gotta admit,
I'm underwhelmed.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.280
Where do you think
they keep their ebay?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.440
RALPH: Beats me.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.520
Hello, anybody here?

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.000
VANELLOPE: Anyone? Hello!

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.840
(ECHOING)
We're looking for ebay!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.960
Ooh. Did you hear that, kid?
Sweet echo.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.400
Check this out.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.800
(MIMICS CAWING SOUNDS)

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.440
VANELLOPE: Hoolie-hoo!
Hoolie-hoo!

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.880
Okay, connect to network.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.720
-(KEYBOARD CLACKING)
-Bingo.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.320
Password is "high score"
with a zero instead of an "o."

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.800
Yes.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.360
And we are online.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.280
-VANELLOPE: Hoolie-hoo!
-(RALPH CAWING)

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.840
-VANELLOPE: Hoolie-hoolie-hoo!
-(RALPH CAWING)

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:41.960
VANELLOPE: Ooh, Ralph, look.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.800
Cool. Mood lighting.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.000
(BOTH SHOUT)

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.120
(RALPH GASPS)

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.040
Ahhh! That's a gremlin!
Stay away! It's a gremlin!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.560
It looks like
a tiny Mr. Litwak.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.600
AUTOMATED VOICE:
IP address 415-1037-483.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.720
Oh, cool! Come on, Ralph,
let's follow him!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.160
Hey, wait for me!
Kid, come back! Wait!

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.120
(GRUNTING) Hey!
Don't leave without me!

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.360
AUTOMATED VOICE:
IP address 415-1037-483.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.520
(VANELLOPE SCREAMING)

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.160
Vanellope!

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.680
(YELPS)

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.680
(MUFFLED) I can't breathe.
I don't fit.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.200
(SHOUTING)

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.320
VANELLOPE: Whoo-hoo!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.600
Yeah! Whoo!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.720
(SCREAMING)

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.760
(GRUNTS, GASPING)

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:32.920
Kid!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.680
Ralph! Isn't this great?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.720
No, it is not!

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.360
Whoo-hoo!

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.360
No, no, no.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.480
(DISTORTED SHOUTING)

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.560
Whoa!

